{{About|the game mechanic|the challenge league|Tempest league|the unique bow|the Tempest}}

'''Tempests''' are a game mechanic that causes environmental hazards to appear randomly in an affected [[area]]. Each tempest hazard appears as a swirling vortex of energy that discharges after several seconds to apply certain buffs to both player characters and monsters within it.

==Mechanics==
* Tempests which grant buffs affect players, allies, and monsters within the area of effect, with a base duration of 5 seconds (Resisting Tempests have base duration of 8 second and Resplendent Tempests have a base duration of 20 seconds). Tempests buffs of the same type do not stack; they will instead refresh the duration of the buff.
* Tempests which deal damage affect both players and their allies and monsters (only legacy tempests had these effects).
* Tempest status effects are not affected by modifiers to [[buff]] effect or duration do not affect tempests applied to you.
* An area can only be affected by one type of tempest at a time. If an area were to be given multiple sources of tempest, only one of them will appear in that area.

==Sources==
* Using a {{il|Scarab of Radiant Storms}} adds Resplendent Tempests to the map.
* [[Vaal side area]]s can have the {{c|mod|Area is affected by a Corrupting Tempest}} modifier.
* [[Incursion room]] controlled by [[Topotante, Architect of Storms]] adds a random tempest to the present day [[The Temple of Atzoatl|Temple of Atzoatl]]. The possible type of tempests depends on the room tier.

